{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"random-decayable-armadillo","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Summary\nThe MCP blue-green autodeploy emits `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR {reason: deploy_failed}` (→ `rebar/host:deploy_errors`, which pages the `rebar-autodeploy-errors` alarm) on TWO conditions that are *documented as routine, non-error backoffs that must be kept OUT of deploy_errors*: `port-exhausted` (retire-cap) and low-memory abort. This false-pages the general \"deploys are failing\" alarm during a normal landing burst, when the deploy is in fact correctly, safely deferring.\n\n## Evidence (live, 2026-08-30 ~03:33–04:05 UTC on i-00880b2c7f13527c5)\nDuring a burst of merges, both blue/green MCP ports (8092/8093) were held by un-reaped containers still in their 21-min graceful drain (`docker stop --time 1260`). Each deploy tick logged BOTH markers for the same event:\n```\nAUTODEPLOY_MCP_RETIRE_CAP {reason: port-exhausted, detail: both 8092 and 8093 held by un-reaped mcp containers; not starting a colliding 3rd (cap=3)}\nAUTODEPLOY_ERROR {reason: deploy_failed, detail: component=mcp target=... fail#1..4 backoff=60s..480s}\n```\n`rebar-autodeploy-errors` (deploy_errors, Sum>0 / 4 periods) and `rebar-autodeploy-mcp-retire-cap` BOTH went ALARM. It self-resolved (~04:15 the old container reaped, `b9dd6e3a` cut over, 1 healthy MCP). No outage — MCP served the old build throughout; only the cutover was delayed.\n\n## Root cause\n`infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh`:\n- port-exhausted path (~line 780): `marker AUTODEPLOY_MCP_RETIRE_CAP port-exhausted ...; record_mcp_backoff_failure; exit 1`\n- low-mem path (~line 771): `marker AUTODEPLOY_MCP_MEM_ABORT ...; record_mcp_backoff_failure; exit 1`\n- `record_mcp_backoff_failure` (~line 547) calls `err deploy_failed \"component=mcp ...\"` → emits `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR` → inflates `deploy_errors`.\n\nThis contradicts the documented contract in `infra/scripts/observability.sh` (mcp blue-green counters): the retire-cap and mem-abort markers are \"each kept out of AUTODEPLOY_ERROR so a routine retire-cap / memory abort never inflates deploy_errors.\" The SUSTAINED case is already covered by the dedicated `mcp_retire_cap` / `mcp_mem_abort` alarms (\"Sustained = releases not draining / a stuck container\"), so the `deploy_errors` emission on these paths is both wrong and redundant.\n\n## Standing intent — this is a fix, not a behavior decision\nThe intended behavior is documented in observability.sh (routine retire-cap/mem-abort kept out of deploy_errors, dedicated alarms cover the sustained case). The code simply doesn't match it. No ADR / design decision required.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n1. A routine `port-exhausted` (retire-cap) backoff does NOT emit `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR/deploy_failed` and does NOT increment `deploy_errors`; the `AUTODEPLOY_MCP_RETIRE_CAP` marker + `mcp_retire_cap` metric remain the signal.\n2. A routine low-memory abort likewise does NOT inflate `deploy_errors`; `AUTODEPLOY_MCP_MEM_ABORT` + `mcp_mem_abort` remain the signal.\n3. GENUINE MCP deploy failures (build-failed, tag-failed, run-failed, unhealthy) STILL emit `deploy_failed` and page `deploy_errors` (no regression to real-failure alarming).\n4. The mcp backoff throttle (timer/prune) still applies on the routine paths so ticks don't hammer during a drain — only the erroneous deploy_errors emission is removed.\n5. A regression test asserts the observable outcome: the retire-cap/mem-abort paths emit their own marker but NOT `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR`, while a real failure emits `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR`.\n\n## Notes\nCheck for duplication against the blue-green target ticket (`panicky-sylphish-foxterrier`) and the MCP graceful-drain-contract bug (`wounded-resident-bushbaby`/b580) before implementing; if already covered, close as duplicate. Fix likely factors the backoff-timer bookkeeping out of the deploy_errors emission in `record_mcp_backoff_failure` (or adds a routine-backoff variant that skips `err deploy_failed`).","id":"6ada-6015-8ac3-44f5","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["infra","autodeploy","mcp","observability","misleading-signal","ready-to-fix"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Autodeploy MCP routine backoff (retire-cap port-exhausted / mem-abort) inflates deploy_errors, false-paging the general deploy alarm"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788065418785021617,"uuid":"fa8f48bd-0ec8-49f5-bd40-9f4fbf5f7801"}